ons and so her thinking was to  give someone else in this case a cake a  who was Michals anointed heir to really  make their own mark on the CDU and to  decide what direction the Conservatives  here in Germany want to go in ahead of  the next elections which at the moment  are set to take place and by autumn of  2021 and so there certainly seems to be  a sense of disappointment from akk a  sense that she feels like she's been let  down and of course I think that was also  made clear over the weekend as well when  Angela Merkel during her trip to South  Africa spoke out about this scandal in  Thuringia and made it very clear on her  opinion on this and that it was simply  something that couldn't be undone the  fact that the CDU the Conservatives have  indeed cooperated with the AFD although  that appointment in that controversial  appointment in Thuringia has fallen  through but the fact is that they did  cooperate with the FT and that simply  cannot be undone and by Mackel voicing  her opinion on that that was also a real  blow to akk and I think that was the  first indication that she might indeed  stand down so she's feeling somewhat let  down we'll continue a conversation in  just a moment but let's first take a  look at the tough fear that on a grid  cramp Karen Bower has had as a CDU party  leader it was all smiles to begin with  in December 2018  annaclaire Crump Karen Bower was elected  as Marcos successor a CDU party leader  the former salon state premier was  Merkel's hand-picked heir and firmly set  her sights on one day filling her shoes  as Chancellor her appointment as German  defense minister soon after was a chance  to prove her worth in a high office but  within her first year as CDU party  leader cracks began to show after a  number of gaffes a joke at carnival  mocking gender-neutral bathrooms sparked  opera from germany's LGBTQI community  toilets these are for men who can't yet  decide whether they want to stand or sit  while peeing while just we